  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Would you be able to sleep with one eye open?",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bottlenose dolphins can.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When they sleep, only half of their brain goes to sleep.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "They sleep with one eye open to stay safe.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Half of their brain sleeps for about two hours before the other half gets a chance to sleep.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Dolphins are not fish—they are mammals.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "The smallest dolphin is about 50 kilos heavy, while the largest kind of dolphin weighs up to 10 tons.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "These mammals have lungs.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "They have to go to the surface of the water to get fresh air.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "These energetic animals can be seen near the coast, sometimes swimming alongside boats.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "Dolphins don't lay eggs.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "Their young are born alive, and they drink milk from their mothers.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "Dolphins are smart and brave.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "Some dolphins save people from shark attacks.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "They are able to solve many problems and even use tools to catch fish.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "But their cleverness doesn't end there.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Dolphins can also pass on anything they learn to other dolphins.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "They show great teamwork.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "They communicate with each other using sounds like whistles and clicks.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-19.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "text": "Maybe they make sentences just as humans do!",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-20.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "text": "Dolphins know the \"voices\" of other dolphins and even know exactly from whom the sounds are.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-21.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "text": "They can also know themselves in a mirror and check different parts of their bodies in it.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-22.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "text": "However, dolphins have been facing danger from humans.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-23.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "text": "There are people shooting them with their guns, causing wounds that make them bleed to death.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-24.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "text": "We should protect the smart animal for a better future, not only for theirs, but also for ours.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-25.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
